 Apache Iceberg Sink V2 for Flink allows automatic execution of maintenance tasks after data is committed to the table, using the addPostCommitTopology(...) method.
 
+Maintenance tasks can be enabled through write options. Each task type has its own `enabled` flag:
+
+| Option | Default | Description |
+|--------|---------|-------------|
+| `rewrite-data-files.enabled` | false | Enable post-commit compaction (rewrite data files). The legacy key `compaction-enabled` is deprecated but still accepted as an alias. |
+| `expire-snapshots.enabled` | false | Enable post-commit snapshot expiration. |
+| `delete-orphan-files.enabled` | false | Enable post-commit orphan file deletion. |
+
+Each task's tunable parameters can be set using the corresponding maintenance config keys (for example `flink-maintenance.expire-snapshots.retain-last` or `flink-maintenance.delete-orphan-files.min-age-seconds`).
+
